From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: add the DSPP 3D LUT of sc8280xp

The DSPPs of sc8280xp have a 3D LUT block ahead of PCC that the driver
does not know about. Describe it in the catalog and add its flush bit.

Its 13-point mode keeps two LUT banks and maps each input channel onto
the grid through a table of breakpoints and slopes. Writing the inactive
bank does not disturb the picture, and the switch is one opmode write
that takes effect with the flush, so a LUT can change between two frames
without tearing. Rewriting the single bank of the 17-point mode while
scanning out does tear, about one frame in five switches here.

Add ops to load a bank with a uniform input map and to select a bank.
The layout was worked out on the hardware: the tables cannot be read
back, so each node's entry was located through the encoder CRC.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
